  "id": "LAW-0478",
  "slug": "contract-formation-10-mechanism",
  "title": "Digital acceptance, without a rule — a screen shows terms before a user action is recorded, on two lanes",
  "titleEs": "Aceptación digital — Mecanismo o relación explicada",
  "category": "contract-formation",
  "categoryName": "Formación del contrato",
  "motif": "Aceptación digital",
  "treatment": "mechanism",
  "family": "spatial-mechanism",
  "description": "A time-lane diagram: Party A's lane and Party B's lane, the supplied order running along both. Party A's screen (●) and Party B's action device (◆), at equal weight, each run on a solid line from the sender's lane to the other lane; only the supplied relationships are drawn (plain relations without arrowheads; nothing causal unless supplied). Then the screen opens first — generic placeholder term rows and a generic button, a scroll rail drawing past each row — and only after it the action device opens (the same button, pressed: the action recorded, as supplied). A tracer follows the supplied traversal order; the focus element swells. A supplied status \"presentation to be examined\" draws a dashed pending ring round the indicated device — a supplied, pending question only. No rule on online acceptance and no legal effect is stated.",
  "tags": [
    "screen",
    "terms shown",
    "user action",
    "action recorded",
    "presentation to be examined",
    "lanes",
    "sequence",
    "relations",
    "tracer"
  ],
